    "answer": {
      "short": "6 dark chocolates, 18 milk chocolates and 12 white chocolates.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of dark chocolates. The numbers of milk and white chocolates are $3x$ and $2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+3x+2x&<40\\\\6x&<40\\\\x&<\\frac{20}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe greatest integer value of $x$ is $6$. Therefore the maximum numbers are $6$ dark, $18$ milk and $12$ white chocolates, giving $36$ chocolates altogether.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
